// After a blast: running water washes the rubble. A reservoir drains through a slot down a stepped 1-in-4 rock
// channel into a tailings pond. On two of its steps lie heaps of loose rubble, as a charge leaves it: iron ore
// lumps at the back, sand and gravel in front of them. The current carries every grain of sand and gravel down
// the steps into the pond; the iron ore is too heavy for it and stays where it lay (a grain of it
// nudged a tile at most). No water is lost.
map
